PlaceRemainder [SimTalk]
Sets where the remainder of the elements of the factory walls or the fence designated by <Path> is to be
added.
Remarks
The remainder is the difference between the length of the wall/fence and the next lower multiple of the
element width.
Note
The attribute is available for graphics of type FactoryWalls and Fence, compare InternalGraphicType.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PlaceRemainder:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify one of the following settings:
PlaceRemainder [SimTalk]
12-1004 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Setting Remainder is located Looks like this
"Clockwise" clockwise at the end of the wall
"Counter-clockwise" counter-clockwise at the end of the
wall
"Top and left" at the top and the left end of the
wall
depends on the orientation of the
wall
"Top and right" at the top and the right end of the
wall
depends on the orientation of the
wall
PlaceRemainder [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1005
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Setting Remainder is located Looks like this
"Bottom and left" at the bottom and the left end of
the wall
depends on the orientation of the
wall
"Bottom and right" at the bottom and the right end of
the wall
depends on the orientation of the
wall
Note
When you change the setting for Placing The Remainder, Plant Simulation resets the Cutouts.
Examples
MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default").createFactoryWalls([11,40,3], 
42cm).PlaceRemainder := "Counter-clockwise"
MyStation1._3D.getGraphic("default").createFence([3,4,1], true, 
false).PlaceRemainder := "Top and left"
